      "reason": "The manuscript does not distinguish between studies excluded because outcomes were not measured versus those excluded because results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Table 4 summarises the primary outcomes of first pass ETI success and overall ETI success for studies with a simulation design without video technology [17, 18, 23-26]. ... Table 5 summarises the primary outcomes of first pass ETI success and overall ETI success for studies with a simulation design with video technology [19, 22]. ... Two studies [20, 21] were included in our meta-analysis of bougie versus stylet first pass ETI success for prehospital studies without video technology ... Two studies [14, 15] were included in our meta-analysis of bougie versus stylet first pass ETI success for prehospital studies with video technology",
      "reason": "The manuscript clearly defines the groups used for synthesis (prehospital vs. simulation, video vs. no video) and links them to the outcomes being analyzed."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_15",
      "quote": "This review aimed to focus exclusively on the prehospital efficacy of these devices to guide the practice of prehospital personnel in their unique setting, thus inclusion of hospital-based RCTs was deemed inappropriate.",
      "reason": "The manuscript provides a clear rationale for the restriction against including hospital-based RCTs."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

